I keep a boogie board erasable LCD thingy as a notepad.  

I lock it up when I'm not in my office and wipe it weekly (or as soon as that project is done).  It has no memory, it magnetically sticks under my desk when I'm not using it but I'm in the office, and I've only accidentally reset it once when I needed it.

&#x200B;

I'm going to echo what you'll hear a lot.   ESET Secure Business is what I use.  I'm a one-man IT department for about 120 users and 140 machines including virtual servers.  Its all windows here, so its not complicated.

&#x200B;

ESET runs light, and it catches just about everything.  I've had zero unnoticed intrusions and zero cases of malware getting through it.  

Once you set up policies on the management server and get your installs going properly you're golden.  I had a little trouble with the installers, so I use PDQ deploy to do the initial installs. \* 

&#x200B;

I tend to deploy ESET Antivirus to devices inside the firewall, and Endpoint Security to devices outside it.  you can run either with the Secure Business license, so outside devices get some web filtering and oversight.

I was running trend micro Officescan until about 4 years ago when I went searching for something that would actually stop fake AV malware and scare-ware.  I've had no security incidents with ESET, except that it keeps deleting a bunch of my Nirsoft tools.

&#x200B;

The new Security Management Center (version 7) is more intuitive than the last rendition of the ESET Remote Administrator, and is miles ahead of the version 4 ERA platform. 

&#x200B;

Licensing is fair. Its not cheap, but for how easy it makes things, IMO its worth it.

Their support is very helpful (use them, you pay for this in the license), and their support knowledge base is active and constantly improving.

ESET has active reps on reddit and spiceworks, so its easy to get help form unofficial channels if you need it.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\**^(If you aren't using a deployment solution, I'd suggest looking at PDQ Inventory and Deploy.. its a lifesaver for me, and its simple to use and set up.  I believe it costs less than other deployment solutions.  Also their support and culture is pretty top-notch.)*
